            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="TIE01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>George</forename>
                        <surname>Tierney</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1761-03-20">
                        <placeName>Gibraltar</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1830-01-25"/>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Godwin first meets George Tierney (1761-1830)  
    at <persName key="LAU01">Lauderdale's</persName> and <persName key="DEB01">Debrett's</persName> in 1796 and most
    of the first contacts are at these venues. In 1798 he meets him with R Johnson (someone also
    associated with<persName key="COU01">John Courtenay</persName>), and in 1799 and 1801 there are connections to <persName key="SHE04">Sheridan</persName> and
    <persName key="BUR02">Burdett</persName>. Godwin also records meeting Tierney on a number of occasions not associated with
    others.</p>
                        <p>Godwin enters him in the 1796 lists under 1796, which is when he enters the diary.<lb/>
  
  Godwin records his death.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
